the planner used in this is the NavFn global planner. it runs a dijikstra/A* algorithm over the entire grid. we do gridbased planning on the costamap. 

local planner ideology used is the mppi controller. which runs a sampling based local planning algorithm. 

looking at the below part of our file :

controller_server:
  ros__parameters:
    controller_plugins: ["FollowPath"]
    FollowPath:
      plugin: "nav2_mppi_controller::MPPIController"
      motion_model: "Omni"

we can say that we are using nav2_mppi_controller::MPPIController as the FollowPath plugin 

mppi is the sampling based version of mpc. it samples candidate trajectories. scores them, executes the first part of the best scored path. then repeats the cycle again.

essentially, the smac planner would be a better choice for a planer as it respets minimum turning radius at the cost of computtion. the NavFn works as a cheap alternative. 

motion_moddel omni is a bad choice as it ignore kinematic feasibility and generates a lot of unfeasible paths , we can solve this by changing the motion model to ackermann.
